NO WRITTEN ENTRANCE EXAM OF ANY KIND. This is a document-plus-interview selection, not a test-based one. Specifically: 
- NO unibz admission test; 
- NO TOLC (TOLC-I, TOLC-E or otherwise) — TOLC applies to unibz BACHELOR engineering programmes, not to this master; 
- NO CENT-S; 
- NO SAT, GRE or GMAT, and no GMAT/GRE bonus of the kind the Master in Accounting and Finance operates; 
- NO portfolio and no written motivation letter with a character limit (unlike the Design/Art programmes). 
The only assessment events are: 
(1) THE ORAL INTERVIEW. Content, verbatim: 'Successful performance in an oral interview aimed at verifying basic knowledge in applied thermodynamics, heat transfer, electrical engineering, and fluid machinery.' It is one of three ALTERNATIVE ways of demonstrating adequate personal preparation — a candidate who already meets criterion (a) or (b) does not necessarily sit it — but the Early Bird non-EU ranking list refers to it as 'the mandatory interview' and lists non-participation as a ground for exclusion, so non-EU candidates in particular should assume they will be called. The Committee may additionally require an interview 'In case the documents included in the online application do not allow the Admission Committee to adequately evaluate the application', held 'in person or via videoconference'. 
(2) THE ENGLISH LANGUAGE EXAM at the unibz Language Centre — only needed if the candidate cannot prove B2 English by certificate or by medium of instruction. Online. Early Bird sittings: 16/03/2026 and 16-17 and 20-21/04/2026; Late sittings: 22-26/06/2026 and 27/07/2026. 
(3) THE OPTIONAL VIDEO PRESENTATION (max 3 minutes, in English, uploaded to YouTube as unlisted, link pasted into the application form) — a scored element, not a test. 
[uncertain] No interview dates are published anywhere on unibz.it for this programme; candidates are contacted individually by e-mail. The programme's own 'study regulation', to which the admission text defers for the interview rules, was not locatable in English on unibz.it.
